# M17 stream packet whose TYPE field flags encryption (FR-2.5).
#
# Identical to reflector-stream.hex except for the TYPE field. Present so the
# tests can prove an encrypted stream parses and is reported UNPLAYABLE — this
# library never decrypts, and exposes no key material or cipher selection.
#
#   bytes 18-19  00 15         TYPE, 16 bits (M17 spec Part I Table 3.2):
#                                bit  0    = 1  stream mode
#                                bits 1-2  = 10 voice
#                                bits 3-4  = 10 AES (Part I Table 3.5)
#                                bits 5-6  = 00 128-bit key (Table 3.6)
#                                bits 7-10 = 0  CAN
#                                bit  11   = 0  not signed
#                              0x0015 = 0b0000_0000_0001_0101.
#
# Every other byte is as documented in reflector-stream.hex, including why the
# frame is 54 bytes rather than Table 27's 56 (OQ-7). Total 54 bytes.
4D313720 1234 FFFFFFFFFFFF 0000009FDD51 0015 0000000000000000000000000000 0001 000102030405060708090A0B0C0D0E0F BEEF
